4. Routes (routes/web.php)
Public:

Method	URI	Action	Name
GET	/	closure → welcome	
GET	/page/{slug}	PageController@show	pages.show
GET	/posts	PostController@publicIndex	posts.index
GET	/posts/{slug}	PostController@publicShow	posts.show
GET	/category/{slug}	PostController@publicByCategory	categories.show
Admin (group: middleware('auth'), prefix('admin'), name('admin.')):

GET /admin/pages etc. — Route::resource('pages', PageController::class)

Route::get('posts/drafts', [PostController::class, 'drafts'])->name('posts.drafts') — before the resource

PATCH posts/{post}/toggle → PostController@togglePublish — name admin.posts.toggle — before the resource

POST posts/upload-image → PostController@uploadImage — name admin.posts.upload_image

Route::resource('posts', PostController::class)

Route::resource('categories', CategoryController::class)

Menu: GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /menu

Settings: GET/PUT /settings

Breeze:

GET /dashboard → redirect to admin.pages.index

/profile — edit/update/destroy

/auth/* — from routes/auth.php

5. Data model
Model	Table	Columns used by app	Notes
Page	pages	title, slug, content, is_published, is_admin_only	casts booleans
Post	posts	title, slug, body, is_published, image_path, category_id	slug unique, nullable
Category	categories	name, slug	hasMany posts
MenuItem	menu_items	title, url, page_id, order	belongsTo Page; accessor target_url
Setting	settings	key, value	key-value store
User	users	standard Breeze	
Important: Post uses body for content (not content). slug is stored and unique — PostController::store()/update() compute it from title.

Public URL note: publicShow($slug) fetches all posts and matches slug (as a fallback it also computes slug from title if the slug column is empty).

6. Layouts
Two parallel layouts. Each is used by a distinct set of pages. Do not mix them.

layouts/admin.blade.php
Used by @extends('layouts.admin') + @section('content')

Contains an @php block reading $globalSettings (or querying Setting::pluck)

@include('partials.theme-vars') renders CSS variables and body/heading styling

@include('layouts.navigation'), then @yield('content'), then @stack('scripts')

Contains CKEditor content styling and admin-panel-specific CSS

layouts/app.blade.php
Used via <x-app-layout> component (App\View\Components\AppLayout)

Same @php block, same partial include

Uses {{ $slot }} — not @yield('content')

Has @isset($header) block for named header slot

Rule: any blade using <x-app-layout> must pass content as a slot. Any blade using @extends('layouts.app') + @section('content') will render blank, because there is no @yield('content') in that layout. Use <x-app-layout> or switch to @extends('layouts.admin').

layouts/navigation.blade.php
Shared nav. Uses $globalSettings for site name and header styling, and $headerMenuItems for the dynamic menu (set by AppServiceProvider).

partials/theme-vars.blade.php
Contains raw CSS (no <style> wrapper) that outputs the CSS variables and applies them to body, headings, and .bg-primary/.text-primary/button[type="submit"] etc. Included inside the <style> block of both layouts.

7. CKEditor 5 setup
Installation
bash
npm install ckeditor5 @ckeditor/ckeditor5-style @ckeditor/ckeditor5-font \
  @ckeditor/ckeditor5-alignment @ckeditor/ckeditor5-highlight \
  @ckeditor/ckeditor5-list @ckeditor/ckeditor5-source-editing \
  @ckeditor/ckeditor5-show-blocks
All GPL-licensed. No premium packages.

Initializer — resources/js/ckeditor-init.js
First two lines (essential):

js
import 'ckeditor5/ckeditor5.css';
import 'ckeditor5/ckeditor5-content.css';
licenseKey: 'GPL'

Exposes window.initCkEditor(selector, options)

Merges options.simpleUpload for image uploads

Attaches a form submit listener that syncs editor content back into the <textarea>

Full toolbar

Blade pattern (four files)
blade
@push('scripts')
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/build/assets/ckeditor-init-<HASH>.css">
<script type="module">
    import('{{ Vite::asset("resources/js/ckeditor-init.js") }}').then(() => {
        window.initCkEditor('#body', {
            simpleUpload: {
                uploadUrl: '{{ route("admin.posts.upload_image") }}',
                headers: { 'X-CSRF-TOKEN': '{{ csrf_token() }}' }
            }
        }).catch(err => console.error('[CKEditor] init failed', err));
    }).catch(err => console.error('[CKEditor] module load failed', err));
</script>
@endpush
Field targets:

File	Target
admin/pages/create.blade.php	#content
admin/pages/edit.blade.php	#content
admin/posts/create.blade.php	#body
admin/posts/edit.blade.php	#body
Why <link> plus dynamic import()
Vite splits dynamically imported modules into separate JS and CSS chunks. Loading only the JS leaves the CSS unloaded, and the editor renders with oversized unstyled icons. The explicit <link> on the CSS chunk fixes it.

The <link> hash changes on every npm run build. After a rebuild, update the hash in all four blades:

powershell
$manifest = Get-Content public\build\manifest.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
$css = "/build/" + $manifest.'resources/js/ckeditor-init.js'.css[0]
$blades = "resources\views\admin\pages\create.blade.php","resources\views\admin\pages\edit.blade.php","resources\views\admin\posts\create.blade.php","resources\views\admin\posts\edit.blade.php"
foreach ($f in $blades) {
    $c = Get-Content $f -Raw
    $c = $c -replace '/build/assets/ckeditor-init-[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.css', $css
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText((Resolve-Path $f), $c, (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding $false))
}
php artisan view:clear
vite.config.js
js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import laravel from 'laravel-vite-plugin';

export default defineConfig({
    plugins: [
        laravel({
            input: [
                'resources/css/app.css',
                'resources/js/app.js',
                'resources/js/ckeditor-init.js'
            ],
            refresh: true,
        }),
    ],
    optimizeDeps: { include: ['ckeditor5'] },
    build: { commonjsOptions: { include: [/ckeditor5/, /node_modules/] } },
});
8. Theme / settings system
Settings page
admin/settings/index.blade.php. Form posts to PUT admin.settings.update. Fields:

settings[site_name] — string

settings[primary_color] — native color input, default #2563eb

settings[accent_color] — default #f59e0b

settings[text_color] — default #1f2937

settings[header_bg_color] — default #ffffff

settings[heading_font], settings[body_font], settings[border_radius], settings[container_width] — dropdowns

header_image — file upload

remove_header_image — checkbox

How theming works
Settings stored in settings table (key / value).

Both layouts read $settings and @include('partials.theme-vars').

The partial outputs CSS variables (--primary-color, --accent-color, --text-color, --heading-font, --body-font, --border-radius) and rules:

css
body { color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); }
h1..h6 { font-family: var(--heading-font); }
button[type="submit"], .btn-primary { background-color: var(--primary-color) !important; }
tailwind.config.js maps classes to variables:

gray.700, gray.900 → var(--text-color)

blue.500, blue.600, blue.700 → var(--primary-color)

indigo.500, indigo.600, indigo.700 → var(--primary-color)

amber.500, amber.600 → var(--accent-color)

What now responds to settings:

text_color → body copy and headings, and every text-gray-700 / text-gray-900 / bg-gray-700 / bg-gray-900 element

primary_color → every bg-blue-600, text-blue-600, bg-indigo-600, text-indigo-600, hover:bg-blue-700, etc. Also button[type="submit"] on admin

accent_color → amber-500/amber-600 classes

heading_font, body_font → applied to body and h1..h6

What does NOT respond: border_radius, container_width, header_bg_color (this one is used in layouts/navigation.blade.php directly).

9. AppServiceProvider (inferred, not seen)
From behavior, it shares two variables with all views:

$globalSettings — array of all settings

$headerMenuItems — menu items for the navigation

If you share this file at the start of a future session, the picture is complete.

10. Everything fixed during this project
Initial CKEditor work:

invalid-license-key with CDN trial key → moved to self-hosted GPL build.

window.initCkEditor is not a function → the <script type="module" src> tag emitted by @vite wasn't executing; replaced with inline <script type="module"> that does a dynamic import().

Stale compiled views → Remove-Item -Recurse -Force storage\framework\views\*.

Old UMD code still in four editor blades → overwritten.

layouts/app.blade.php referenced a nonexistent /js/ckeditor-init.js → removed.

Blank <x-app-layout> pages → @yield('content') changed to {{ $slot }}, added @isset($header).

CKEditor icons huge → added <link> on the CSS chunk in four blades (Vite splits dynamic imports).

$accentColor undefined → stale compiled view.

admin/posts/edit.blade.php loaded the pages edit form → overwritten.

Global text color setting did nothing → added body { color: var(--text-color); }, mapped Tailwind gray.

Structural cleanup:

Five admin blades broken (wrong layout + nonexistent routes) → converted to @extends('layouts.admin') with correct admin.* route names:

admin/categories/edit.blade.php

admin/posts/create.blade.php (was the pages create form)

admin/posts/edit.blade.php

admin/posts/drafts.blade.php

admin/posts/show.blade.php

Post::$fillable had slug before the column existed → column added via migration, all posts backfilled with unique slugs.

Post.php wiped by broken PowerShell → restored, no BOM.

Ran the full task-priority list (rebuild+hash, deleted dead controllers, fixed CSS typo, converted categories index, added slug, wired Tailwind colors, extracted partial).

Theme CSS extracted to partials/theme-vars.blade.php. First version had nested <style> tags causing raw CSS to render as text — fixed by removing the wrapper.

Drafts route was missing (removed by earlier commit 19c3437 that replaced manual routes with Route::resource). Added back with correct ordering.

Admin PostController::index() filtered to published-only → removed the filter so /admin/posts shows everything.

Added PATCH admin/posts/{post}/toggle route + Publish/Unpublish button to the index. The togglePublish() method already existed.

admin/categories/index.blade.php had an HTML typo: onsubmit attribute was missing a space before it in one form → fixed by rewriting the blade.

Multiple BOM issues from Set-Content -Encoding UTF8 → fixed with WriteAllText(..., UTF8Encoding $false).

11. Working conventions and gotchas
PowerShell BOM trap
Set-Content -Encoding UTF8 writes a byte-order mark (BOM) at the top of the file. For .php files this causes:

Namespace declaration statement has to be the very first statement

For .blade.php, .js, .css, .json — safe with Set-Content.

For .php — use this instead:

powershell
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($path, $content, (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding $false))
Or for line-based edits:

powershell
(Get-Content $path) -replace 'old', 'new' | Out-File $path -Encoding utf8NoBOM
(utf8NoBOM requires PowerShell 6+.)

Verifying no BOM in app/
powershell
Get-ChildItem -Path app -Recurse -Filter *.php | ForEach-Object {
    $bytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($_.FullName)
    if ($bytes.Length -ge 3 -and $bytes[0] -eq 0xEF -and $bytes[1] -eq 0xBB -and $bytes[2] -eq 0xBF) {
        Write-Host "BOM found: $($_.FullName)"
    }
}
Empty output = clean.

Verify file was written
Always add a size or content check at the end of a file-writing command:

powershell
Write-Host "Written. Size: $((Get-Item $path).Length) bytes"
Because Set-Content on an empty $content writes zero bytes and reports no error.

Layout rule
@extends('layouts.admin') + @section('content') → admin pages

<x-app-layout> + <x-slot name="header"> → public pages

@extends('layouts.app') + @section('content') → does not work (no @yield('content') in that layout)

Blade cache
After editing a blade:

powershell
php artisan view:clear
If changes still don't appear:

powershell
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force storage\framework\views\* -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
php artisan optimize:clear
Server restart
php artisan serve (PHP's built-in server) caches loaded controller classes. After editing a controller, restart the server. Blades don't need this.

File naming trap
Three create.blade.php files exist (pages/, posts/, categories/). Same for edit.blade.php. VS Code tabs show only the filename. Use Ctrl+P and type part of the path, or expand the folder and click from inside it.

Debugging blank pages
View Page Source (Ctrl+U) first, before opening DevTools. Laravel fatals show as empty HTML with no console error. The php artisan serve terminal prints the request line even when Laravel logs nothing.

